# Age-Bias-Corrected SN Cosmology: Cobaya Modifications

This repository provides modified components of **Cobaya v3.5.1** for Markov Chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) sampling with an age-bias-corrected Type Ia supernova (SN Ia) likelihood.

The modifications were developed for the cosmological analyses presented in:

**Son et al. (2025)**  
*Strong Progenitor Age-bias in Supernova Cosmology. II. Alignment with DESI BAO and Signs of a Non-Accelerating Universe*  
[arXiv:2510.13121](https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.13121)

---

## 1. Code Description

This repository contains selected components of [Cobaya v3.5.1](https://pypi.org/project/cobaya/3.5.1/) that have been modified to incorporate an age-bias correction into the SN Ia likelihood analysis.

The following directories contain the relevant implementations:

- `likelihoods/` — Modified likelihood modules.
- `theories/` — Modified theory modules.

These modifications enable MCMC sampling using the age-bias-corrected SN Ia likelihood.

## 2. Installation & Usage

**Step 1. Install Cobaya v3.5.1**

Install Cobaya version 3.5.1 in your Python environment.

`pip install cobaya==3.5.1`

**Step 2. Replace the corresponding directories**

Locate the installed Cobaya package directory (`cobaya/`).

Replace the following directories in your Cobaya installation with the corresponding directories provided in this repository:

**Note:** Back up the original directories before replacement. These modifications were developed for Cobaya v3.5.1, and compatibility with other versions is not guaranteed.

## 3. Environment Reproducibility

The `cobaya_env.yml` file provides the Conda environment used for the cosmological analyses presented in **Son et al. (2025)**.

To recreate the environment, run:

`conda env create -f cobaya_env.yml`

This environment is provided to facilitate reproducibility of the published analyses.

## 4. Reproducing the Results

The `example/` directory contains example input files for reproducing the cosmological analyses and results presented in **Son et al. (2025)**.

